From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:24:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: Fix stack corruption when handling logind suspend
 signals

dbus_message_get_args() writes a dbus_bool_t (four bytes) for a
DBUS_TYPE_BOOLEAN argument, but the PrepareForSleep handler stores it in a
plain C bool, which is one byte. The three surplus zero bytes land in the
adjacent stack slot, which on some compilers is the saved %rbx of
dbus_logind_handler() -- the register holding the caller's DBusConnection
pointer. The low three bytes of the connection pointer are then zeroed, and
the CONNECTION_LOCK() that dbus_connection_dispatch() performs directly
after the filter returns dereferences the resulting page-aligned address,
killing the daemon on every suspend.

Declare it as dbus_bool_t, matching the type the API expects (and the one
already used for the polkit reply in this file).

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
---
 rtkit-daemon.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rtkit-daemon.c b/rtkit-daemon.c
--- a/rtkit-daemon.c
+++ b/rtkit-daemon.c
@@ -1708,7 +1708,7 @@ static DBusHandlerResult dbus_logind_handler(DBusConnection *c, DBusMessage *m,
 static DBusHandlerResult dbus_logind_handler(DBusConnection *c, DBusMessage *m, void *userdata) {
         if (dbus_message_is_signal(m, "org.freedesktop.login1.Manager", "PrepareForSleep")) {
                 DBusError error;
-                bool active;
+                dbus_bool_t active;
 
                 dbus_error_init(&error);
                 if (dbus_message_get_args(m, &error, DBUS_TYPE_BOOLEAN, &active, DBUS_TYPE_INVALID)) {
